<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.25in; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">As
the Group&#8217;s loans and related payable to investors do not trade in an active market with readily observable prices, the Group uses
discounted cash flow methodology involving significant unobservable inputs to measure the fair value of these assets and liabilities,
including discount rates, net cumulative expected loss rates, and cumulative prepayment rates. Financial instruments are categorized as
